# API Information


main: {
  kit: {
    info: {
      contact: {
        email: "engineering@artic.edu"
      }
      description: "An API for an aggregator of Art Institute of Chicago public data. This documentation was generated by `php artisan docs:openapi` on 2026-03-23 12:06:11"
      servers: [
        {
          url: "https://api.artic.edu/api/v1"
        }
      ]
      termsOfService: "https://www.artic.edu/terms/terms-and-conditions"
      title: "Art Institution of Chicago API"
      version: "1.14"
      tagline: "Explore the Art Institute of Chicago's public collection — artworks, artists, exhibitions, galleries, and IIIF images"
      homepage: "https://api.artic.edu/docs/"
      docs_url: "https://api.artic.edu/docs/"
      license_short: "Mixed CC0 / CC-BY 4.0 depending on the resource; images via IIIF, public-domain works recommended"
      license_md: `- Most metadata is released under a Creative Commons Zero (CC0) 1.0 designation.
- Artwork descriptions are licensed CC-BY 4.0; places data is CC-BY with attribution to the Getty Thesaurus of Geographic Names.
- Images are served via the IIIF Image API 2.0; the docs recommend only using images of works tagged as public domain, and users remain responsible for individual copyright status.
- Use is subject to the museum's [terms and conditions](https://www.artic.edu/terms/terms-and-conditions).`
      about_md: `The Art Institute of Chicago API is a read-only aggregator of public data from the [Art Institute of Chicago](https://www.artic.edu/), exposing the museum's collection, programming, and editorial content over a single JSON HTTP interface rooted at \`https://api.artic.edu/api/v1\`.

What you get from the API:

- Collection records — artworks, the agents (artists, makers, organisations) connected to them, the places and galleries where they live, and the controlled vocabularies that describe them.
- Programming and editorial — exhibitions, events, tours, articles, press releases, digital and printed publications, educator resources, and static site pages.
- Media — IIIF-backed images plus videos, sounds, and texts associated with the above.
- Search — every resource type has its own \`/search\` endpoint, and a unified \`/search\` endpoint queries across the whole dataset with faceting, pagination, and sorting.

No authentication is required for basic use. Anonymous clients are throttled to roughly 60 requests per minute per IP; the docs ask that you send an \`AIC-User-Agent\` header identifying your project and a contact email, and direct higher-volume users to engineering@artic.edu. Most endpoints have CORS enabled and listings default to sorting by last-updated descending.`
      entity_desc: {
        agent: "A person or organisation (artist, maker, donor, etc.) related to collection records. Exposed at `/agents`, `/agents/{id}`, and `/agents/search`."
        agent_role: "A controlled vocabulary describing how an agent relates to an artwork (e.g. artist, donor)."
        agent_type: "A classification of agents (individual, corporate body, and so on)."
        article: "Editorial articles published by the museum."
        artwork: "An object in the museum's collection — paintings, sculptures, prints, and so on. Exposed at `/artworks`, `/artworks/{id}`, and `/artworks/search`."
        artwork_date_qualifier: "Controlled vocabulary qualifying how an artwork's date is interpreted (circa, before, after, etc.)."
        artwork_place_qualifier: "Controlled vocabulary qualifying how an artwork's place relates to it (made in, found in, etc.)."
        artwork_type: "Classification of artworks by medium or form (painting, drawing, sculpture, etc.)."
        category_term: "Hierarchical category and classification terms used to tag collection records."
        digital_publication: "A digital publication produced by the museum."
        digital_publication_article: "An individual article within a digital publication."
        educator_resource: "Teaching resources made available for educators."
        event: "A scheduled public event at the museum."
        event_occurrence: "A specific dated instance of a recurring event."
        event_program: "A program grouping related events."
        exhibition: "Past, current, and upcoming exhibitions. Exposed at `/exhibitions`, `/exhibitions/{id}`, and `/exhibitions/search`."
        gallery: "Physical galleries within the museum building. Exposed at `/galleries`, `/galleries/{id}`, and `/galleries/search`."
        generic_page: "Generic CMS-managed pages on the museum website."
        highlight: "Curated highlight entries promoting selected content."
        hour: "Opening-hours records for the museum."
        image: "Media records for images, served through the IIIF Image API 2.0. Exposed at `/images`, `/images/{id}`, and `/images/search`."
        landing_page: "Landing pages on the museum website."
        place: "Geographic places associated with collection records; uses the Getty Thesaurus of Geographic Names."
        press_release: "Museum press releases."
        printed_publication: "Print publications such as books and catalogues produced by the museum."
        product: "Products listed by the museum (for example shop items referenced in editorial content)."
        publication: "Publication records that may span print and digital formats."
        search: "Unified cross-resource search endpoint at `/search`, plus per-resource `/{resource}/search` endpoints supporting facets, pagination, and sorting."
        section: "Sections within larger publications or site structures."
        site: "Site grouping used to scope content across artic.edu properties."
        sound: "Audio media records associated with collection or editorial content."
        static_page: "Static informational pages on the museum website."
        text: "Text media records (essays, labels, and other written content)."
        tour: "Self-guided or curated tours through the collection."
        video: "Video media records associated with collection or editorial content."
      }
      auth: false
    }
  }
}
